 "editorial_note": "GitHub listed fifteen projects this Friday morning, and eight of them were already featured here in the past week. Of the rest, four stood out. LZ4's first release in over two years ==brings multithreaded compression into the library itself==. Vercel's agent-browser gives coding agents a text-first browser, Google publishes an official set of agent skills for its cloud, and Microsoft's VibeVoice turns hour-long recordings into speaker-labelled transcripts. Curation order reflects practical interest, not GitHub rank. Trending is not a release date or an endorsement.",
 "coverage_notes": [
  "All 15 listing entries were inspected. Exact public GitHub API metadata and recent releases were checked for all fifteen at about 07:02 UTC, and README files for six; every checked repository was active and unarchived. GitHub's API detects Apache-2.0 or MIT for three picks; for lz4/lz4 it reports NOASSERTION, and the repository's LICENSE file was read to establish the split BSD-2-Clause / GPL-2.0-or-later licensing.",
  "No repeats. Eight entries featured before were left out without a material change since their last pick: NVIDIA/auto-ontology, vercel-labs/agent-desktop and JiaFeiMiao-K-Cat/DiscImageStudio (5 November), floci-io/floci and Usagi-org/ai-goofish-monitor (4 November), D4Vinci/Scrapling and max-sixty/worktrunk (3 November) and mattpocock/skills (31 October). Auto Ontology, agent-desktop, Floci, ai-goofish-monitor, worktrunk and mattpocock/skills have had no release since; Scrapling's v0.5.1 was already weighed on 5 November; Disc Image Studio's v1.4.1 and v1.4.2 add translations and a CD burning fix for some drives, judged incremental.",
  "New entries not picked: garrytan/gstack (a personal Claude Code skill set, close to setups covered before, also left out on 5 November), scenario-labs/skills (agent skills that mostly need a paid Scenario account, also left out on 5 November) and ConardLi/garden-skills (six design, video and retrieval skills, a smaller overlap with today's google/skills pick).",
  "No security-focused project was on today's list.",
  "The preceding seven calendar dates, 30 October-5 November, were checked for local history; all seven editions exist.",
  "The official listing was captured at 08:01:21 Europe/Paris. Literal stars-today labels are GitHub's displayed period figures; API total stars and README evidence were checked separately at the times shown per card. They are not an independently audited rolling 24-hour growth measurement.",
  "Speed, accuracy and capability descriptions are the maintainers' own, including LZ4's benchmark tables and VibeVoice's transcription length, language count and real-time figures. No candidate code, installer, skill, plugin, browser or model was installed, downloaded or run, and none of this is a security audit or endorsement."
 ],
