  {
   "repository": "lz4/lz4",
   "url": "https://github.com/lz4/lz4",
   "trending_rank": 8,
   "description": "The ==reference implementation of LZ4==, the very fast lossless compression format used inside databases, file systems, kernels and network stacks. It ships the liblz4 library (block, frame and file APIs), the lz4 command-line tool and its test suites. Release v1.11.0, published on 4 November, is the first since July 2024 and gathers more than 850 commits.",
   "why_interesting": "First time on our list, and the most foundational project on it. v1.11.0 ==puts multithreaded compression into the liblz4 frame API==: one new field, nbWorkers, and the output stays identical whatever the thread count, so results are reproducible. The release notes also report much faster compression of small blocks and dictionaries, clearer decompression error codes, and new contract tests, mutation testing and fuzzing that found and fixed corner-case bugs.",
   "caveat": "The speed tables (for example roughly 7.5 GB/s with 16 workers at level 1) are the maintainers' own measurements on specific CPUs and compilers. ==nbWorkers is labelled experimental== in this release, and the static library stays single-threaded by default. Licensing is split: ==lib/ is BSD 2-Clause, the CLI and other files GPL-2.0-or-later==, which matters if you embed more than the library. We did not build or run it.",
   "category": "Developer tools / compression library",
   "language": "C",
   "license": "BSD-2-Clause (lib) and GPL-2.0-or-later (other files)",
