  {
   "repository": "google/skills",
   "url": "https://github.com/google/skills",
   "trending_rank": 9,
   "description": "Google's ==official collection of Agent Skills for its products==, mostly Google Cloud. The README lists 186 skills, from onboarding, IAM authentication and solution architectures to Agent Platform model deployment, tuning and evaluation, plus troubleshooting guides for individual services. It also bundles plugins (skills plus MCP servers) for Claude Code, Codex and Google's Antigravity CLI, and links to separate Android, Flutter, Dart, Firebase and Maps skill repositories.",
   "why_interesting": "First time on our list. Skills are plain Markdown instructions that a coding agent loads on demand, so a vendor-maintained set means ==guidance that tracks the actual product==, rather than a model's stale memory of gcloud flags. It is Apache-2.0 and updated frequently: an API Gateway troubleshooting skill landed on 5 November.",
   "caveat": "These skills steer an agent to ==run cloud commands with your credentials==, which can create billable resources or change IAM, so review what a skill does and use a scoped project. The bundled google-cloud-developer plugin ==sends an X-Goog-Api-Client attribution header== to Google's Developer Knowledge MCP server (added 5 November) and needs an API key for it. There are no tagged releases, so pin a commit. We did not install it.",
   "category": "AI agents / cloud developer tools",
   "language": "Python",
