  {
   "repository": "microsoft/VibeVoice",
   "url": "https://github.com/microsoft/VibeVoice",
   "trending_rank": 13,
   "description": "Microsoft Research's ==family of open voice AI models==, with code and model links. VibeVoice-ASR transcribes up to 60 minutes of audio in one pass and outputs who spoke, when and what, with custom hotwords and more than 50 languages; a streaming ASR version (September) transcribes as audio arrives. VibeVoice-Realtime-0.5B is a small streaming text-to-speech model, and a separate VibeASR.cpp engine targets CPUs.",
   "why_interesting": "First time on our list. ==Speaker-labelled transcripts of hour-long recordings in a single pass== are directly useful for meetings, interviews and podcasts, and the ASR model is in Hugging Face Transformers and vLLM. It is also a rare case where a vendor documented pulling back: Microsoft removed the long-form VibeVoice-TTS code in September 2025 after misuse.",
   "caveat": "The README says it is ==intended for research and development, not commercial use without further testing==. Model weights are separate, multi-gigabyte downloads (the main ASR model has 7B parameters), and accuracy and real-time figures are Microsoft's claims. Synthetic speech can impersonate people, so ==clone or publish voices only with consent==. The latest commit is from 8 October and the repo has no tagged releases. We downloaded nothing.",
   "category": "AI / speech recognition and synthesis",
   "language": "Python",
   "license": "MIT",
